``` Storm-3358 ARTEX Agentic Intrusions Against the Financial Sector
    Field names follow CIM/UDM conventions and have not been tested against live data; adjust them to your environment.
    Splunk hunt, CIM data models (tstats). Author: daniyyell-dev. https://github.com/daniyyell-dev/rapid-threat-intel/tree/main/threats/2026-11_November-2026/2026-11-11/Storm-3358-ARTEX-Agentic-Intrusions-Financial-Sector
    Sources: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/06/artex-abuse-expands-as-cybercriminals-target-financial-sector/
    Published 2026-11-06. Set the time picker to at least the last 30 days, or back to the earliest activity in the sources.
    The indicators below are live and malicious: do not browse to them.
    Needs these CIM data models populated: Network_Traffic, Endpoint, Web. A model with no data simply returns nothing.
    summariesonly=false also reads events the acceleration has not summarised yet. If these data models are
    accelerated, summariesonly=true is much faster but only sees the summary range.
    No CIM? Use hunt_raw.spl with the rti_* macros from all/splunk_macros.conf.
    Output: first_seen, last_seen, ioc, ioc_type, data_model, host, user, src, dest, detail, count

    Behaviours (indicators of attack) are extra sections below, with ioc_type "behaviour (alert)" or "behaviour (hunt)".
    Behaviours are leads, not confirmed indicators, and can match legitimate activity. Compare any hit against your own baseline and environment before acting.
    Behaviours are for hunting and alerting only; never block on them. ```
| tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
    FROM datamodel=Network_Traffic.All_Traffic
    WHERE All_Traffic.dest_ip IN ("199.19.95.66", "199.19.95.67", "199.19.95.68", "91.92.240.238", "85.11.168.45", "85.11.167.52", "178.16.54.129", "31.77.229.35")
    BY All_Traffic.src_ip All_Traffic.dest_ip All_Traffic.dest_port All_Traffic.action All_Traffic.dvc All_Traffic.user
| rename "All_Traffic.*" AS *
| eval data_model="Network_Traffic", ioc_type="ipv4", ioc=dest_ip, host=dvc, src=src_ip, dest=dest_ip, detail="connection to IOC, port ".dest_port.", ".action
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Network_Traffic.All_Traffic
        WHERE All_Traffic.src_ip IN ("199.19.95.66", "199.19.95.67", "199.19.95.68", "91.92.240.238", "85.11.168.45", "85.11.167.52", "178.16.54.129", "31.77.229.35")
        BY All_Traffic.src_ip All_Traffic.dest_ip All_Traffic.dest_port All_Traffic.action All_Traffic.dvc All_Traffic.user
    | rename "All_Traffic.*" AS *
    | eval data_model="Network_Traffic", ioc_type="ipv4", ioc=src_ip, host=dvc, src=src_ip, dest=dest_ip, detail="connection from IOC, port ".dest_port.", ".action
]

``` Behaviour 1 (Alert): Web server starting a downloader or shell
    Look for: A web server process starting curl, wget, nc, ncat, netcat or a shell
    Log source: EDR process events on internet-facing web servers
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Endpoint.Processes
        WHERE Processes.parent_process_name IN ("w3wp.exe", "httpd", "apache2", "nginx", "php-fpm", "php", "java", "node", "tomcat") Processes.process_name IN ("curl", "curl.exe", "wget", "nc", "ncat", "netcat", "sh", "bash", "cmd.exe", "powershell.exe")
        BY Processes.dest Processes.user Processes.parent_process_name Processes.process_name Processes.process
    | rename "Processes.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, src="-", detail=parent_process_name." > ".process, data_model="Endpoint.Processes"
    | eval ioc="Web server starting a downloader or shell", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 2 (Hunt): Rapid scanning with default scanner user agents
    Look for: Bursts of many varied requests from one source in minutes, with default tool user agents (Nmap, curl, wget, Python HTTP clients, headless Chromium or Playwright)
    Log source: Web server, WAF and reverse-proxy logs
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen dc(Web.url) AS paths values(Web.http_user_agent) AS agents
        FROM datamodel=Web.Web
        WHERE Web.http_user_agent IN ("*Nmap*", "curl/*", "Wget*", "python-requests*", "Python-urllib*", "*aiohttp*", "*httpx*", "*HeadlessChrome*", "*Playwright*")
        BY Web.src Web.dest _time span=5m
    | rename "Web.*" AS *
    | where count>=100 AND paths>=20
    | eval host=dest, user="-", detail=count." requests, ".paths." paths in 5m; ".mvjoin(mvindex(agents, 0, 2), " | "), data_model="Web"
    | fields - paths agents _time
    | eval ioc="Rapid scanning with default scanner user agents", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 3 (Hunt): New cron jobs and temp-folder binaries on web hosts
    Look for: New cron jobs, and new binaries run from temporary or world-writable folders, on web hosts
    Log source: EDR process and file events
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Endpoint.Processes
        WHERE Processes.process_path IN ("/tmp/*", "/var/tmp/*", "/dev/shm/*")
        BY Processes.dest Processes.user Processes.parent_process_name Processes.process_name Processes.process
    | rename "Processes.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, src="-", detail="run from a temp folder: ".process, data_model="Endpoint.Processes"
    | eval ioc="New cron jobs and temp-folder binaries on web hosts", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Endpoint.Filesystem
        WHERE Filesystem.file_path IN ("/etc/cron.d/*", "/var/spool/cron/*", "/etc/crontab") Filesystem.action IN ("created", "modified")
        BY Filesystem.dest Filesystem.user Filesystem.file_path Filesystem.file_name Filesystem.action
    | rename "Filesystem.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, src="-", detail="file ".action." ".file_path, data_model="Endpoint.Filesystem"
    | eval ioc="New cron jobs and temp-folder binaries on web hosts", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]
| sort 0 - last_seen
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table first_seen last_seen ioc ioc_type data_model host user src dest detail count

``` Behavioural hunt notes:
    A web-serving process (w3wp.exe, httpd, nginx, php-fpm, java, node) launching curl, wget or netcat is how the ARTEX agents delivered the WISP, vshell and AdaptixC2 RATs.
    Connections from inside your network to the WISP or C2 addresses suggest an implant; inbound hits from ARTEX servers mean probing or exploitation attempts. ```
